Reproduced: a `tests/*_test.rs` file containing a `// test ` marker was lexed as Redblue — `./target/debug/rb test` printed `Failed: 1` / `exit=1`, and `rb test tests/zz_repro_test.rs` named the fault (`LexerError: Unexpected character '>'`). The defect is live, latent today only because no current Rust test file carries a marker.

Fix: `find_test_files` collects only `.rb` (src/testing/mod.rs:69), `run_all_tests` filters `.rb` only (src/testing/mod.rs:47), results sorted for deterministic reporting; `find_test_files` made `pub` (visibility only) so the filter is observable from a test. `rb test` with the same fixture now reports `Failed: 0`, `exit=0`.

Added `tests/discovery_test.rs` — 11 `#[test]` fns, 4 of them `edge_*`, 2 asserting failures (`edge_lexer_rejects_rust_source_sent_to_harness`, `missing_test_file_is_reported_as_an_io_error`). Red-then-green confirmed before the fix.

Gates: fmt pass, clippy `-D warnings` pass, `cargo test` 42 passed / 0 failed. `./rbops/verify.sh` could not run — `rbops/` and `phases/` do not exist in this checkout (`No such file or directory`); stated as not-run in REPORT.md rather than claimed green. `phases/phase-002/REPORT.md` and `FINDINGS.md` written (4 out-of-scope defects filed, including `rb test <path>` exiting 0 on failure and the harness ignoring `test "…" end` blocks).
